- **SIMD Vectorization**: Use Java's Vector API to perform vectorized operations on the arrays, which can accelerate operations such as element-wise additions and multiplications.

**Code Example for Parallelism**:
```java
import java.util.concurrent.ForkJoinPool;

public void parallelTransformInternal(double[] data, int direction) {
    int n = data.length / 2;
    int logn = log2(n);
    bitreverse(data);

    ForkJoinPool pool = new ForkJoinPool();
    pool.submit(() -> {
        for (int bit = 0, dual = 1; bit < logn; bit++, dual *= 2) {
            pool.submit(() -> {
                double[] cosTable = new double[dual];
                double[] sinTable = new double[dual];
                for (int i = 0; i < dual; i++) {
                    double theta = 2.0 * direction * Math.PI * i / (2.0 * dual);
                    cosTable[i] = Math.cos(theta);
                    sinTable[i] = Math.sin(theta);
                }

                for (int b = 0; b < n; b += 2 * dual) {
                    for (int a = 0; a < dual; a++) {
                        int i = 2 * (b + a);
                        int j = 2 * (b + a + dual);

                        double z1_real = data[j];
                        double z1_imag = data[j + 1];

                        double wd_real = cosTable[a] * z1_real - sinTable[a] * z1_imag;
                        double wd_imag = cosTable[a] * z1_imag + sinTable[a] * z1_real;

                        data[j] = data[i] - wd_real;
                        data[j + 1] = data[i + 1] - wd_imag;
                        data[i] += wd_real;
                        data[i + 1] += wd_imag;
                    }
                }
            }).join();
        }
    }).join();
}
```

